+This is a necessity theorem, not an assertion that an accepted abstract pattern
+has polynomial coefficients realizing it. Choices of coefficients or siblings
+that the screen treats independently can introduce false positives, which do not
+damage this implication. One chosen path is insufficient: all mandatory major
+siblings must pass. The three selected-path-only false survivors in paragraph 9
+are a concrete check of that distinction.
