+
+**10. Corrections to the calibration rhetoric and ancillary controls.** A weaker
+necessary screen having 14 extra rows is not a contradiction of Moh's exclusions
+and does not refute coarse (8) as a valid necessary condition. It refutes only the
+claim that this particular coarse screen reproduces his complete reported program
+output. Whether his implementation used the sharper action or additional tests is
+**OPEN as a historical implementation question**. The proof above, not the table
+match, licenses the sharpening beyond n=100.
+
+The five descended p.207 rows all pass the **bottom-residue control** for some
+zero/nonzero reading. At `(21,14;M_2=16;V_2=2)`, C_2=0 gives `(L,A_1)=(1,6)`
+and fails; C_2 nonzero gives `(2,3)` and passes. These rows have Jacobian x or x^2,
